course: dictionary
lesson: 34
title: Acacia, a tree of hot, dry places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An acacia is a noun, a name for a kind of tree or shrub. Its meaning comes from the words around it: «A giraffe's tongue wraps round acacia leaves to pull them from between the thorns.» Thorns are sharp points, so an acacia is a plant with small leaves and spiky bits.
explain: Look for clues about where it lives. Our dictionary says acacias grow in warm, dry places such as Africa and Australia, and the savannah sentences show giraffes eating from them. Try the swap check: «A giraffe ate leaves from a tree» still makes sense, so acacia names a kind of tree.
fact: An acacia is a tree or shrub with small leaves, often thorns, and yellow or white flowers.
fact: Acacias grow in warm, dry places such as Africa and Australia.
fact: In Australia, many acacias are called wattle.
fact: Golden wattle is the national flower of Australia.
fact: Giraffes eat acacia leaves, pulling them from between the thorns with their long tongues.
exercise: «The giraffe pulled leaves from an acacia tree.» What is an acacia? | A type of rock | *A tree or shrub with small leaves, often thorns | A fast animal that lives on the savannah | A sort of bird's nest
exercise: In Australia, many acacias are called what? | Kudu | Savannah | *Wattle | Baobab
exercise: Where do acacias grow? | Cold, wet mountains under deep snow | *Warm, dry places such as Africa and Australia | Deep under the sea | Only inside zoos
test: «Ants living inside the thorns of some acacia trees bite an elephant's trunk, so elephants leave those trees alone.» What does this tell you about thorns? | Thorns are yellow flowers | *Thorns are sharp points on the plant | Thorns are sweet juice | Thorns are soft, green leaves
test: «Whistling-thorn acacias give ants homes in swollen thorns and sweet nectar.» What do the ants get from the acacia? | *A home in the thorns and sweet nectar | Cold water from the roots | Bright yellow petals | Long, dark tongues
exam: Which description best matches an acacia? | A sea animal with eight arms | A grass that grows in cold snow | A tall pine with needles all year round | *A tree or shrub with small leaves, often thorns, and yellow or white flowers
